  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "have to: obligation (review)",
      "title_form": "Have to: obligación (repaso)",
      "title_target": "Have to: obligation (review)",
      "description_md_form": "Usamos **have to** para hablar de **obligaciones** y **requisitos** en el trabajo. Es una forma muy común en contextos laborales.\n\n**Estructura:**\n\n- **Afirmativo:** `Subject + have/has to + verb`\n  - *I have to read the contract.*\n  - *She has to sign the contract.*\n\n- **Negativo:** `Subject + don't/doesn't have to + verb` (no es necesario)\n  - *You don't have to work on Monday.*\n\n- **Pregunta:** `Do/Does + subject + have to + verb?`\n  - *Do you have to work on Saturday?*\n\n**Importante:** Con *he, she, it* usamos **has to**. Con *I, you, we, they* usamos **have to**. En preguntas y negaciones, siempre usamos **have** (nunca *has*).",
      "description_md_target": "We use **have to** to talk about **obligations** and **requirements** at work. It is a very common form in work contexts.\n\n**Structure:**\n\n- **Affirmative:** `Subject + have/has to + verb`\n  - *I have to read the contract.*\n  - *She has to sign the contract.*\n\n- **Negative:** `Subject + don't/doesn't have to + verb` (it is not necessary)\n  - *You don't have to work on Monday.*\n\n- **Question:** `Do/Does + subject + have to + verb?`\n  - *Do you have to work on Saturday?*\n\n**Important:** With *he, she, it* we use **has to**. With *I, you, we, they* we use **have to**. In questions and negatives, we always use **have** (never *has*).",
      "grammar_structure": "Subject + have/has to + base verb",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "have_to_present",
        "headers": [
          "Pronombre",
          "Afirmativo",
          "Negativo",
          "Pregunta"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "I",
            "have to",
            "don't have to",
            "Do I have to...?"
          ],
          [
            "You",
            "have to",
            "don't have to",
            "Do you have to...?"
          ],
          [
            "He/She/It",
            "has to",
            "doesn't have to",
            "Does he/she/it have to...?"
          ],
          [
            "We",
            "have to",
            "don't have to",
            "Do we have to...?"
          ],
          [
            "They",
            "have to",
            "don't have to",
            "Do they have to...?"
          ]
        ]
      },
